      "writtenOn": "2023-02-07T17:57:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a good idea. I didn\u0027t use the parameter tag as index mainly because not all parameter need to define range (for example most enum and boolean parameters), in this case client will need to differentiate default values in ranges vector.\nAlso I\u0027m thinking about how to support nested parameter data structure range, for example, current implementation can not support define range of: HapticGenerator.VibratorInformation.resonantFrequencyHz\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:hardware/interfaces/audio/aidl/android/hardware/audio/effect/HapticGenerator.aidl;l\u003d88\n\nOne way to make it generic enough to handle all parameters range is define Range as:\n```\n@VintfStability\nparcelable Range {\n    Parameter.Id id; // replace int tag;\n}\n\n```\n\nAnd in Capability we still have `Range[] ranges`.\nWhat do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "bca182d4_f5067fe9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 60,
        "startChar": 11,
